{#
/**
 * @file
 * Template for the calendar pages.
 *
 * Available variables:
 * - events: The annual astronomical events, each with 'label', 'class' and 'date'.
 * - sol_headings: The sols of the week, each with 'abbreviation', 'name' and 'weekend'.
 * - months: The 24 months, each with 'number', 'name', 'season', 'image' and 'weeks'. Each week is a list of 7 cells,
 *   each with a 'label' (NULL for an empty square) and a list of 'classes'.
 */
#}
<p>Viewing the calendar in the familiar format of one page per month helps to visualise how a mir is divided into
  months and weeks, and how the weeks align with months. Note how the final week of each quarter is a short, 6-sol
  week.</p>

<p>Nominal dates for the major astronomical events each mir are highlighted. The actual dates of astronomical events
  can vary slightly from these (although usually by not more than 1 sol) due to variations in the Martian tropical
  year, and the intercalation rules not keeping the calendar in precise alignment with Mars&rsquo; orbit. Credit goes
  to Tom Gangale for calculating these dates.</p>

<p>The intercalary sol at the end of a long mir (Tucana 28) is shown in bold.</p>

<table class="utopian-events">
  <caption>Annual Astronomical Events (Nominal Dates)</caption>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Event</th>
      <th>Date</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    {% for event in events %}
      <tr>
        <td>{{ event.label }}</td>
        <td class="special-sol {{ event.class }}">{{ event.date }}</td>
      </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>

<div class="utopian-calendar-pages">
  {% for month in months %}
    <table class="calendar-page {{ month.season }}">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th class="calendar-page__month-name" colspan="7">{{ month.number }}. {{ month.name }}</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td class="calendar-page__month-icon" colspan="7">
            <img src="{{ month.image }}" alt="{{ month.name }} constellation">
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="calendar-page__sols-of-week calendar-page__squares">
          {% for heading in sol_headings %}
            <th{{ create_attribute().addClass(heading.weekend ? 'weekend' : []) }}><abbr title="{{ heading.name }}">{{ heading.abbreviation }}</abbr></th>
          {% endfor %}
        </tr>
        {% for week in month.weeks %}
          <tr class="calendar-page__squares">
            {% for cell in week %}
              <td{{ create_attribute().addClass(cell.classes) }}>{{ cell.label ?? '' }}</td>
            {% endfor %}
          </tr>
        {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  {% endfor %}
</div>
